# Forklift cabin frames and expanded kits

FKC01 replaces Side guards with Cabin frame. The posts, overhead rails and roof are replaced as one independent part, with tubular, pressed, twin-hoop, canted, rounded, cross-braced, canopy, lattice, arched, sport, grid, heavy-duty and safari designs. The original frame remains available. Lamps, mirrors, beacon, operator controls and lifting mast remain on the forklift. The Garage focuses on the upper cabin and places the preview callout there.

FKC02 adds **ten further alternatives to each forklift category**: engine cover, rear guard, wheel covers and cabin frame. Each list now has fourteen choices: Original, three retained IDs and ten new IDs. This adds forty purchasable options. Old `body` IDs (`fork_rail`, `fork_plate`, `fork_twin`) now select cabin designs, retaining the same saved selection and ownership keys. Other vehicles' option tables and all unrelated backend catalogue entries are unchanged.

FKC03 retains independent preview, compare, equip, reset, local save/reload, appearance sync, ownership confirmation, race and ghost construction. New items use the established 750-coin price. The server whitelist includes every option; matching backend deployment is required before new items can be purchased or synced online. No live service was changed.

FKC04 refreshes four forklift base scenes, 104 full/simple kit scenes and its Garage template. These are original procedural assets, with no generated-image or third-party model input. Handling and collision contracts are unchanged. The shared build identity was regenerated by `dev.ps1`; it is excluded from the task-only checkpoint, and must be regenerated through that entry point after applying the patch.

The [native review gallery](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/gallery.html) contains all 56 choices on each desktop renderer. Examples: [arched cabin](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/garage-gl-final/body-fork_arch.png), [canopy](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/garage-gl-final/body-fork_canopy.png), [turbine wheel cover](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/garage-gl-final/rims-fork_turbine.png), and [engine scoop](evidence/forklift-cabin-kits-2026-11-02/garage-gl-final/hood-fork_scoop.png). Final captures wait for both the kit sweep and camera transition to finish. Earlier captures are retained separately and can show the previous part during the sweep.

