The retained sticker failure compares 25 server entries against 13 native entries. Its server list is byte-equivalent as parsed JSON before and after this task. The first backend run lacked `PYTHONPATH`; the next included three unavailable localhost PostgreSQL fixtures. Corrected final commands set the backend import path and explicitly exclude PostgreSQL. No PostgreSQL pass is claimed.

Initial sandboxed Godot commands were denied access to the normal user log directory and Windows certificate store. Completed offline checks used isolated test `APPDATA` and normal Windows process access, with crash-dialog suppression. The first new assertion assumed Godot retained duplicate mesh names (741 checks, 2 failures); checking presence instead gives 741/0. The first Original comparison mixed a batched car with an unbatched legacy body (6 checks, 5 failures). Comparing both raw constructors gives 6/0 without relaxing the geometry, UV or normal requirements. These logs remain in the evidence directory.

